econds; H2 predicts the inverse') requires isolating getfqdn from bind, which nested spans defeat unless getfqdn/server_bind is intercepted directly"],"finding":"The three instrumented spans (constructor, TCP bind, getfqdn) are NESTED, not sequential: CPython HTTPServer.server_bind calls socket.getfqdn(host) from inside the ThreadingHTTPServer constructor (editor.py:511). Sequential timing wrapped around edit_workflow(...) or the constructor cannot separate the getfqdn cost from the constructor/bind cost — yet the H1-vs-H2 discrimination depends on that separation. The plan implies wrapping ('timing around ... the socket.getfqdn call', 'preserve original arguments/return values/exceptions') but does not state the interception point that makes the nested spans separable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8c776e64027ff8bc","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan bullet 2 ('transparent, semantics-preserving timing around the editor server constructor, TCP bind, and socket.getfqdn call')","norm_id":"n9cd847e58843a8f8","priority":0.099,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The organic CI run charges the whole 35s to the constructor span, leaving H1 vs H2 unresolved because getfqdn and bind were not separately measured"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Specify that the _server-fixture instrumentation monkeypatches/wraps socket.getfqdn (and/or the HTTPServer.server_bind path) so the getfqdn elapsed time is captured distinctly from the surrounding constructor/bind time, restoring the original callable afterward.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_expl